               .resume-section-content
                    h2.mb-5 About Me                    
                    
                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            p
                                | I am a Software Engineer at Google on the Android LLVM Toolchain team.
                                | I help maintain and release the Android LLVM Compiler Toolchain to first-party developers and through the Android NDK.
                                | I also contribute upstream to LLVM on behalf of Android, landing fixes and features, and co-organize the LLVM Bay Area Monthly Meetup.

                            p
                                | Previously, I completed my Ph.D. in Computer Science at the Georgia Institute of Technology, advised by <a href="https://www.cc.gatech.edu/people/santosh-pande">Dr. Santosh Pande</a>.
                                | My research spanned the intersection of compilers, programming languages, and systems security.
                                | Before that, I was a Research Assistant at Carnegie Mellon University with <a href="https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~iliano/">Dr. Iliano Cervesato</a> and <a href="http://www.gisellereis.com/">Dr. Giselle Reis</a>, where I also earned my B.S. in Computer Science.

                            p
                                | Outside of work, I enjoy video games (currently Halo Campaign), TV shows (currently The Pitt), manga (One Piece), and trying new restaurants.
                                | I also love to travel — I have visited 25 countries and over 60 cities.
                                | My most recent trips took me across the United States for the FIFA World Cup 2026.

